// CROWN — THE VACUOUS NEGATION. `run`'s body row is its parameter's row,
// a free cell at run's exit, and a declared `!E` over it used to constrain
// nothing: `run(() => op())` compiled clean and ran (exit 7, measured
// 2026-08-18 and again 2026-09-27 on boot 2974547b). The gate now rides
// f's row cell; the argument edge that binds the instance to `[E]` is the
// write that refuses, naming run's declaration. Expect E_EffectMismatch.
effect E { op() -> Int }
handler h { op() => resume(7) }
fn run(f) with !E = f()
fn main() = (run(() => op())) ~> h
